-- Hand-built, deliberately VALID instance of NQueens.use (SOIL statements,
-- no Kodkod search) -- 8 queens on an 8x8 board (matching NQueens.properties'
-- [small] section), placed according to an independently-computed N=8
-- solution.
--
-- "Independently-computed" here means: a plain Python backtracking search
-- (self-written for this fixture, ~40 lines, ordinary depth-first placement
-- with a diagonal/column safety check per candidate) run completely outside
-- this repository's plugin -- no Kodkod, no USE, no `mv -validate`, and not
-- the witness this suite's own solver run happens to find. That independence
-- from the thing under test is the entire point of a validating fixture in
-- this suite (see docs/kk-modelvalidator-port.md and the exact same pattern
-- in GraphColoring/valid-instance.soil). The search enumerated all 92
-- distinct N=8 solutions (a well-known count, reproduced here as a sanity
-- check on the search itself) and the first one found by plain depth-first
-- order was kept:
--   row -> col:  0->0, 1->4, 2->7, 3->5, 4->2, 5->6, 6->1, 7->3
-- i.e. as a permutation indexed by row: [0, 4, 7, 5, 2, 6, 1, 3]. Verified
-- independently (same script) that no two of these 8 (row,col) pairs share
-- a row, a column, or either diagonal.
--
-- Per NQueens.use's modeling approach, row/col are NOT attributes directly
-- on Queen: each Queen is linked via the mandatory 1-1 QueenRow/QueenCol
-- associations to its own Row and Col object, and row/col distinctness is
-- structural (a total 1-1 association between two equal-size, fully
-- populated classes is a bijection), not an extra OCL invariant. So this
-- fixture creates 8 Row objects (idx 0..7, one each, matching the queen's
-- row above), 8 Col objects (idx 0..7, one each), 8 Queen objects, and then
-- links each queen to its own row and its own col per the permutation above.
--
-- Every invariant in NQueens.use (distinctRowIdx, distinctColIdx, noAttack)
-- should report OK against this state -- see valid-instance.cmd.

!create row0 : Row
!set row0.idx := 0
!create row1 : Row
!set row1.idx := 1
!create row2 : Row
!set row2.idx := 2
!create row3 : Row
!set row3.idx := 3
!create row4 : Row
!set row4.idx := 4
!create row5 : Row
!set row5.idx := 5
!create row6 : Row
!set row6.idx := 6
!create row7 : Row
!set row7.idx := 7

!create col0 : Col
!set col0.idx := 0
!create col1 : Col
!set col1.idx := 1
!create col2 : Col
!set col2.idx := 2
!create col3 : Col
!set col3.idx := 3
!create col4 : Col
!set col4.idx := 4
!create col5 : Col
!set col5.idx := 5
!create col6 : Col
!set col6.idx := 6
!create col7 : Col
!set col7.idx := 7

!create queen0 : Queen
!create queen1 : Queen
!create queen2 : Queen
!create queen3 : Queen
!create queen4 : Queen
!create queen5 : Queen
!create queen6 : Queen
!create queen7 : Queen

!insert (queen0, row0) into QueenRow
!insert (queen1, row1) into QueenRow
!insert (queen2, row2) into QueenRow
!insert (queen3, row3) into QueenRow
!insert (queen4, row4) into QueenRow
!insert (queen5, row5) into QueenRow
!insert (queen6, row6) into QueenRow
!insert (queen7, row7) into QueenRow

!insert (queen0, col0) into QueenCol
!insert (queen1, col4) into QueenCol
!insert (queen2, col7) into QueenCol
!insert (queen3, col5) into QueenCol
!insert (queen4, col2) into QueenCol
!insert (queen5, col6) into QueenCol
!insert (queen6, col1) into QueenCol
!insert (queen7, col3) into QueenCol
